# Local backend override — LOCAL USE ONLY, do not commit an activated copy.
#
# The committed providers.tf declares a remote azurerm backend (Azure Storage,
# AAD/OIDC) so the plan-on-PR job can read shared state. That backend needs a
# storage account / container / key at `terraform init`, so a bare `terraform
# init` on a laptop prompts for a container name and can't be run offline.
#
# Terraform automatically merges any file ending in `_override.tf`, and a
# `backend` block in an override *replaces* the primary one. Copy this file to
# `backend_local_override.tf` to swap the azurerm backend for local state so you
# can stand the endpoint up and tear it down from your own machine with no Azure
# Storage account and no prompts:
#
#   Copy-Item backend_local_override.tf.example backend_local_override.tf
#   terraform init
#   terraform plan
#   terraform apply
#
# `backend_local_override.tf` and `terraform.tfstate*` are gitignored, so this
# stays local and never disturbs the remote-backend config CI relies on.

terraform {
  backend "local" {}
}
